language 0.1.0
module infrastructure
  means
    Provided and managed technical resources forming the computing foundation
    on which a software system is placed and runs.

entity resource : thing
  means
    resource: a managed technical entity providing computing, network or disk
    capability for the running of a system.

entity host : thing
  means
    host: a physical or virtual computing system able to run software
    processes.

entity cluster : thing
  means
    cluster: a group of hosts or other homogeneous resources managed as a
    single whole.

entity container : thing
  means
    container: an isolated execution environment sharing the kernel of the
    operating system with other such environments.

entity region : thing
  means
    region: a geographically defined area holding the infrastructure resources
    of one provider.

entity zone : thing
  means
    zone: a part of a region isolated with respect to failures.

entity volume : thing
  means
    volume: an addressable resource of persistent block or file storage,
    attachable to a computing environment.

entity resource-quota : thing
  means
    resource quota: an established upper boundary of the available or consumed
    amount of an infrastructure resource.

entity provider : thing
  means
    provider: a subject or system providing infrastructure resources and
    managing their underlying environment.
